oakMOSS: a charger plugged in after a DAC is not held at 100 mA.

The USB manager's rmmod_device_driver() (the port left device role, as it does for a DAC)
writes INPUT_CURRENT_LIMIT = 0 through the AXP2202 USB supply. axp2202_set_iin_limit clamps
that to its 100 mA floor (code 0 of IIN_LIM, 0x17), and the property write marks the limit as
claimed, so the adapter state machine skips its pmu_usbad_cur write (2500 mA in the DT). That
machine is re-armed only by the usb-in interrupt, and a DAC swapped for a charger gives it no
VBUS edge: the board charged at 100 mA, below its own draw, and the gauge fell on the charger
(Zero 28, 2026-11-27: IIN_LIM 0x17 = 0x80, 5 V 2.4 A brick, 27 -> 25 % with the screen on).

A write of 0 now clears the claim and re-arms the state machine five seconds out (the delay the
usb-in interrupt uses), so pmu_usbad_cur applies unless a host enumerates and claims 500 mA
first. Any other write is as before. The work is only touched once probe has initialised it,
and only with BC1.2 off, where it exists. axp2202_usb_get_property also masks bit 7 (the BC1.2
switch), so sysfs reports the real limit instead of 6500.

--- a/lichee/linux-4.9/drivers/power/supply/axp2202_usb_power.c
+++ b/lichee/linux-4.9/drivers/power/supply/axp2202_usb_power.c
@@ -126,7 +126,8 @@
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
-	data = (data * 50) + 100;
+	/* bit 7 is the BC1.2 switch, not a current step (it read back as 6500 mA) */
+	data = ((data & GENMASK(5, 0)) * 50) + 100;
 	val->intval = data;
 
 	return ret;
@@ -286,6 +287,22 @@
 
 	switch (psp) {
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_INPUT_CURRENT_LIMIT:
+		if (!val->intval) {
+			/* The USB manager writes 0 when the device-mode driver goes
+			 * (rmmod_device_driver: the port became a host). That is not
+			 * a request for the 100 mA floor, and no host has claimed the
+			 * port: leave the limit alone and let the adapter state
+			 * machine apply pmu_usbad_cur again. Without this a charger
+			 * plugged in after a DAC, with no VBUS edge for the usb-in
+			 * interrupt to act on, stayed at 100 mA. The work exists only
+			 * once probe has set it up, and only with BC1.2 off. */
+			atomic_set(&usb_power->set_current_limit, 0);
+			if (!usb_power->dts_info.pmu_bc12_en &&
+			    usb_power->usb_chg_state.work.func)
+				mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &usb_power->usb_chg_state,
+						 msecs_to_jiffies(5 * 1000));
+			break;
+		}
 		ret = axp2202_set_iin_limit(regmap, val->intval);
 		atomic_set(&usb_power->set_current_limit, 1);
 		break;
